{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner correction of the complete R3 first draft at exact head43b68f5a6d1f1a68bcb494062fa2db0e081f7ef9, handoffc2408d90. I read all888 lines of notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md (56110 bytes,SHA-256f2f78fb0db14cfdb8f4a99580d97b5916cad533c90b7a9c6ff4035357fc45483) and all723 lines of publication-and-authority-facts.md (84111 bytes,SHA-25612db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0). The two-file diff against maine6 passes whitespace checking. I also checked the bounded original source anchors mints.ts1–35, workspaces.ts20–58 and ref-fence.ts146–172 at d691. The source reading remains evidence of an earlier candidate, not verified deployment behavior, current adoption or a complete source audit. No tests, builds, installs, provider probes, credential operations or deployments were run.\n\nThe direct-membership observation choice, distinct task/member identities, irrevocable destination reservation, exact compare-and-swap retry, asynchronous receipt write and preserved uncertain external duties are useful design foundations. Nine corrections follow; they keep the full browser/cloud/device outcomes and all-component retirement obligations.\n\n1. Complete and qualify D2's authority proof. The held observation must bind the exact membership ScopeRef/incarnation, key/member, action/resource extent, issuing delegation/grant and grantor key/member, controller relation, profile/version and observed head; retain its inputs for replay. Current authority includes active grantor/member, permitted action and resource, and grant expiry at commit, not just an active signing key and role. Either define bounded delegations fully or state an owned explicit deferral; a principal member alone cannot account for which revoked issuing device authorized a delegation. State the ordering and clock checks: observation time cannot be in the future of the commit, negative age never proves freshness, raw clock regression requires reacquisition/refusal, and time-limited grants are checked at commit. Use a conservative read-start time or account explicitly for read duration; do not call the bound10 seconds while permitting20. Label the proposed grace windows as product/protocol choices, including cached acceptance after revocation, not instantaneous current authority. The race table must cover revocation after observation but before reservation and compromise notification delayed or lost. Reconcile 'fresh authority before every write' with 'reservation is irrevocable': later ordinary retirement cannot both allow completion and forbid the only required dispatch credential. State what authorizes service settlement/receipt/fencing writes and what a post-reservation compromised revocation stops. Rules observations need the same retained domain/freshness treatment. Numeric budgets remain R4 proposals, not measurements.\n\n2. Finish browser/device/private-resource authority. Bind read tokens to the repository/membership incarnation, audience, key/member, permitted read scope and expiry; one deployment checking secret must not make a token for repository A authorize B. Document read-session grace after revocation consistently: section9's 'a revoked device reads nothing' conflicts with ten-minute cached read tokens, and already-open streams need an enforcement deadline rather than only request-time checks. Do not imply recall of bytes already displayed. Private reads, checkpoint export, task control and raw fork credentials require the controller's or admin's direct active device authority; delegated member/admin handles are insufficient, as plan005/C1 requires. Specify signed request domain, resource, action, body digest, nonce/operation identity, notAfter, replay and exact outcome recovery, including exports whose reply is lost. Carry client-held non-extractable device keys, single-use authorized enrollment, invitation custody, last active admin-key guard, recovery-key enrollment/rotation and removed-member refusal explicitly. Removing the last owner key must stop new agent tools as well as lane acts, within a stated boundary, while admitted effects reconcile. A new device must not silently apply an unsent act from a different device as durable work. Keep ownerMayReview as a qualified controller exception; it never exempts a reviewer who is an author or a principal behind the contribution.\n\n3. Reconcile task/hold/workspace identities with plural commitments and the complete checkpoint contract. R2 revision2 handoff3265ebe at f146aa2e explicitly asks for a fork per commitment; R3 still assigns a fork per lane. Different accepted commitments in the same issue lane cannot share writable refs or environments, and replacement/holder-change environments must not expose a former holder's private dirty work. Name exact lane/commitment/hold/epoch/runtime-instance/incarnation ownership and never-reused provider names. An expired fork token or refused later report is not a filesystem fence for a still-running process, nor proof an older push cannot overwrite a reused fork ref. Define tool-dispatch/write fencing, old runtime quiescence and controlled restore/export; keep old unknown operations separate. Retention must cover task records and conversation, dirty/deleted/untracked/ignored files, modes/links, prepared Git object closure, command intents/output/observed exits, atomic checkpoint receipt guards and last-good recovery, not 'work is saved' alone. R0/C2's staged successor owns the complete environment experiment, without a new probe here. State deadline start/extension/active renewal, failed or corrupt save/restore, running-process reattachment versus loss, unknown-effect pins and legal retention roots, owned deletion/tombstone/failed retry. A review-window request after fulfilled commitment cannot simply reopen a final item: show successor work or the proper unfinished commitment. These are dependencies with named owners, not a claim R3 alone implements storage.\n\n4. Correct the ledger's settlement rule. Sections2,5.3 and8 currently let a complete inventory started after a request settle unknown creates. Their own facts4.2/4.3 and the original source directly contradict that: an unknown credential/repository create can apply after any listing, and occupancy is not that attempt's answer. A complete inventory can account for known/answered resources and support cleanup; it cannot prove an earlier in-flight or unknown operation ended. Retain that operation until its own authenticated completion/refusal or a separately established completion fence. A later retry gets its own identity/name and cannot discharge the earlier duty. Known token expiry ends only that known token's cleanup, never a mint with unknown identity/expiry or an in-flight push. Preserve canonical no-unattributed-token revocation and fork/snapshot provenance rules; 'complete inventory' is not permission to revoke unrelated canonical credentials. Update E1/reset conditions and the outside-effect table, including imports, deletes and check-job deadlines: deadline can end eligibility/scheduling, not prove external execution/cleanup or command side effects ended. Safely resolved cleanup stays independent of publication slot release and ordinary receipt delivery.\n\n5. Express publication as correlated protocol messages under R1. R1 now permits one terminal result per request; R3 sends reserved, unresolved and published as multiple results for one request, so the two drafts cannot execute together. Choose a compact request/result plus source-owned progress/terminal relationship-update scheme, or explicitly revise R1 with justified semantics. Give source/target ScopeRefs, operation fact and ordinal, destination owner revisions, deduplication, out-of-order handling and final outcome consumption. A late 'reserved' must not revert published, and lost receiver storage is unknown, not R1's unsafe undeliverable terminal release (current correctionf4ed2dab). Freeze every eligibility-bearing source item from intended, including review comments if they mutate verdict, new request-changes, review withdrawal/dismissal, live job selection/check results, manifest, plan/conditions and exact closure-link set. R2's corrected design is the basis, not the earlier superseding-comment/check model. Show cancel before request delivery, queued cancellation racing reservation, source restart with lost result, malformed/wrong-target progress, and destination retry after a terminal reply is lost. The destination derives required approvals/checks, qualifications and blocking request-changes from the pinned complete source eligibility commitment; an arbitrary supplied subset of 'counted' facts is not proof that nothing blocks. Distinct member identity prevents two enrolled keys from counting as two reviewers.\n\n6. Make dispatch/abort evidence describe every possible send. A publisher invocation may forward multiple POSTs under a reusable gateway grant, and a detached process or lost callback may keep running. 'Every attempt has a refusal/not-sent report' is terminal proof only if an attempt accounts for all of its actual sends and the owned writer can no longer dispatch under it. State durable pre-dispatch intent, runtime-instance/gateway fencing, grant closure and exact accepted refusal/not-dispatched evidence. A generic exec failure/timeout, container loss, token revocation or HTTP403 after send is unknown. An uncertain mint can be push-not-sent if no dispatch occurred, but its credential duty remains unknown. Qualify the measured upload-revocation behavior rather than assert a host guarantee. Readback may confirm the operation's exact aggregate effect while attribution among earlier unknown identical attempts remains unknown; do not invent per-attempt answers or discard token debt. Retain read evidence and its host/read route as verification input. Give the admission-time/job-key/tree/config/sandbox-output contract for checks and actual job origin verification, including retry and late-result correlation, rather than relying on the existence of a lane fact alone.\n\n7. Complete the publication and proposed abort-fence assumptions. Exact expected-old compare-and-swap is supported by the Git command contract (official https://git-scm.com/docs/git-push, checked today); that documentation is not an Artifacts-specific server/read guarantee or a bound on delayed writes. Old value must never be reused while an older write could still arrive: an external writer can otherwise move base→other→base and resurrect the aborted write. State exclusive destination ownership across incarnations/deployments and allowed admin adoption/reset, and how a foreign-writer incident preserves quarantine/unknown duties rather than treating today's different ref as permanent proof. H2 also needs the effect of a stale integration/fence read, not only a stale base read; replay reports the resulting host consistency trust. An abort-fence is a concrete proposal for existing design review, not an additional owner-approval ceremony. Specify its exact deterministic commit/operation identity, first parent/tree, service authorization despite the compromised key, ledger/token/writer duties, exact readback, restart/retry, source outcome, updated destination head and receipt/attention. The original push and fence race must both be shown. It does not 'always end' without eventual host/observation availability; outstanding unknowns remain visible. Until a complete fence contract is adopted, retaining the slot is the honest rule.\n\n8. Finish object staging and receipt ownership. An integration cannot merely be required to exist in canonical objects without an owned, authorized object-import/pin/staging path. Name the issuer, source fork/commitment/epoch, read token, ref-fenced canonical credential, durable attempt and cleanup for all selected contributions and prepared integration objects. Exact selected commits/trees and combined assembly must satisfy 